<header><p class="enc-kicker">Term · currency</p><h1 class="enc-title">CFA franc</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1945</span> · Also known as West African CFA franc, Central African CFA franc</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The CFA franc is the name of two currencies used in West and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-africa">Central Africa</a>, created by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in December 1945 for its African colonies. After independence it survived as the West African CFA franc and the Central African CFA franc, each issued by a regional central bank, pegged first to the French franc and since 1999 to the euro and guaranteed by the French Treasury.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cfa-franc.jpg" alt="CFA franc" width="320" height="253" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jarry1250 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CFA_Franc_map.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
